Short:        HarfBuzz 15.1.0 text shaping library
Author:       Serkan Dursun
Uploader:     Serkan Dursun <EMAIL>
Type:         util/libs
Version:      15.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.1.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     68020+, AmigaOS 3.1+

harfbuzz.library is HarfBuzz 15.1.0 (2026), the OpenType text shaping
engine used by Firefox, Chrome, LibreOffice and Android, as a shared
library for AmigaOS 3. It comes from AAText (util/wb/AAText) but is a
library for any program.

A program gives it a font and a line of Unicode text; HarfBuzz answers
which glyphs to draw and where:
- kerning from the GPOS table (most fonts made since about 2010 have
  no other kerning),
- ligatures (fi, ffl) and other OpenType features (small caps, old
  style figures, ...), switched on and off per call,
- accents placed on their letters,
- Arabic and Hebrew (right to left), the scripts of India and South-East
  Asia, Hangul, and every other script HarfBuzz knows.
Drawing the glyphs is up to the program (FreeType, freetype2.library or
anything else); harfbuzz.library does not need FreeType.

Built with HB_MINI: OpenType shaping only (no 'kern' table, no Apple
AAT, no Graphite, no subsetting or glyph drawing). TrueType, OpenType/
CFF, collections and variable fonts. 126 functions of the HarfBuzz API,
called exactly like HarfBuzz on any other system: the headers in
Developer/include make each call a jump through the library vector.

- All calls are serialised by one semaphore, so any number of tasks may
  use the library.
- Memory from an exec pool; a call runs on a 32 KB stack of its own when
  the caller has less than 12 KB left.
- Output is the same as HarfBuzz 15.1.0 on a PC (tested); 532 malformed
  fonts of HarfBuzz's fuzzing set: no crash, no leak.
- Speed (WinUAE, 68060 JIT, 16 px): about 2400 lines of 78 characters
  per second with Source Sans 3, 7500 with DejaVu Sans.

Installation
  Copy Libs/harfbuzz.library LIBS:
(Libs/harfbuzz.library.060 is the 68060 build, copy it as
LIBS:harfbuzz.library; the .debug build prints to the serial port.)

For programmers
Developer/include: proto, inline and fd headers and the HarfBuzz
headers. Developer/examples/hbshape.c is a complete example:

  m68k-amigaos-gcc -m68020 -O2 -noixemul -Iinclude -o hbshape examples/hbshape.c

Tests/: hbshape, hbinfo, hbbench, hbfuzz. Details in
harfbuzz_lib_EN.txt (Turkish: harfbuzz_lib_TR.txt).

License: HarfBuzz "Old MIT" (LICENSE.harfbuzz.txt), its Universal
Shaping Engine data MIT, Microsoft (LICENSE.ms-use.txt); the library
around it MIT (LICENSE.txt). Source: https://github.com/Sdursun/AAText
